    {
      "id": 62018,
      "name": "Zalrus9",
      "username": "Zalrus9",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/zalrus9/{size}/2124_2.png",
      "created_at": "2013-04-28T20:43:06.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Phantom5613\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantom5613/48/1906_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Phantom5613:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Sorry, never watched DHSAB. <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/confused.png?v=12\" title=\":confused:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":confused:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>You should, at least once, and it should be rather easy to find. Speaking as a person who has been in a live production of it, it's okay, but by no means is it the greatest thing since sliced bread and oh we should continue worshiping at the feet of Joss Whedon oh he can do no wrong… But I digress.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>But yeah, Both of the sides of Mad Bomber Blade are very concurrent with the story of DHSAB; at first he's in front of recoding equipment of some sort, and next he has his death ray of sorts. Also, since some of Tachyon's quotes are shout-outs to that show (\"Dude, I'm not your nemesis,\" \"Look at my wrist…\" That sort of thing) I would think it's safe to say there was some inspiration taken from there.</p>",
      "post_number": 4,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:38:30.214Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
      "incoming_link_count": 0,
      "reads": 0,
      "readers_count": 0,
      "score": 0.0,
      "yours": false,
      "topic_id": 7836,
      "topic_slug": "mad-bomber-art",
      "display_username": "Zalrus9",
      "primary_group_name": null,
      "flair_name": null,
